.*
.* WRKOUTQ: every output queue, or the spooled files on one. The
.* columns sit where the V7R1M0 captures have them
.* (golden/verified/oracle71/panels); a queue's status comes one
.* column in from its heading, as the driver gives it.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 6'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 4'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=QSTSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=CNTCL BASETYPE='ZONED 4 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PTYCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VIEWCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=QUEUE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=FILES CLASS=CNTCL.
:VAR NAME=WRITER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=STATUS CLASS=QSTSCL.
:VAR NAME=FILE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USRDTA CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=STS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=PAGES CLASS=CNTCL.
:VAR NAME=COPIES CLASS=CNTCL.
:VAR NAME=FORMTYPE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=PTY CLASS=PTYCL.
:VAR NAME=JOB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=NUMBER CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=SPLNBR CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=QSTS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=FVIEW CLASS=VIEWCL VALUE='1'.
:COND NAME=VIEW1 EXPR='&FVIEW. EQ "1"'.
:COND NAME=VIEW2 EXPR='&FVIEW. EQ "2"'.
:LISTDEF NAME=QUEUES VARS='OPT QUEUE LIB FILES WRITER STATUS'.
:LISTDEF NAME=FILES VARS='OPT FILE USER USRDTA STS PAGES COPIES FORMTYPE PTY JOB NUMBER SPLNBR'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/OQKEYS' NAME=OQKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:EKEYL.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/FILEKEYS' NAME=FILEKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=VIEW1.F11=View 2
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=VIEW2.F11=View 1
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F20 ACTION='CMD WRKWTR'.F20=Writers
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='CMD WRKWTR'.F22=Printers
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=QUEUES KEYL=OQKEYS HELP=WRKOUTQ ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with All Output Queues
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=QUEUES.(No output queues)
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGOUTQ OUTQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDOUTQ OUTQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.3=Hold
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?DLTOUTQ OUTQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKOUTQ OUTQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.5=Work with
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSOUTQ OUTQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.6=Release
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKOUTQD OUTQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.8=Description
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ENTER='CMD WRKWTR'.9=Work with Writers
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=14 ENTER='CMD CLROUTQ OUTQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.14=Clear
:LISTCOL HELP='QUEUES/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/QUEUE' VAR=QUEUE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=10.Queue
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIB' VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=25.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/FILES' VAR=FILES USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=43.Files
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/WRITER' VAR=WRITER USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=54.Writer
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/STATUS' VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=69.Status
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=FILES KEYL=FILEKEYS HELP=WRKOUTQ ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Output Queue
:DATA DEPTH=2 COMPACT.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/QUEUE' VAR=QUEUE USAGE=OUTPUT.Queue
:DATAIX VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT.
:DATAIXT.Library
:DATAIX VAR=QSTS USAGE=OUTPUT.
:DATAIXT.Status
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=FILES VIEWS=2.(No spooled output files)
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ENTER='CMD ?SNDNETSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.1=Send
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGSPLFA FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.3=Hold
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD DLTSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.5=Display
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.6=Release
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=7 ENTER='CMD DSPMSG'.7=Messages
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKSPLFA FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.8=Attributes
:LISTACT HELP='FILES/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ENTER='CMD WRKWTR'.9=Work with printing status
:LISTCOL HELP='FILES/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/FILE' VAR=FILE USAGE=OUTPUT.File
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/USER' VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT.User
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/USRDTA' VAR=USRDTA USAGE=OUTPUT.User Data
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/STS' VAR=STS USAGE=OUTPUT.Sts
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/PAGES' VAR=PAGES USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=49.Pages
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/COPIES' VAR=COPIES USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=57.Copies
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/FORMTYPE' VAR=FORMTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=65.Form Type
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/PTY' VAR=PTY USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=77.Pty
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JOB' VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=49.Job
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/NUMBER' VAR=NUMBER USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=61.Number
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT FILE USER USRDTA STS PAGES COPIES FORMTYPE PTY'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT FILE USER USRDTA STS JOB NUMBER'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2, 3 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKOUTQ.Work with Output Queues - Help
:P.Output queues with the files waiting on them and the writer that
prints them; option 5 shows a queue's files. F11 switches between the
files' printing attributes and the jobs that made them.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/OQKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QUEUES/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/QUEUE'.Queue
:P.The queue of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FILES'.Files
:P.The files of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WRITER'.Writer
:P.The writer&colon. the job that prints the spooled files of an output
queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QUEUES/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Output Queue (CHGOUTQ) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Output
Queue (HLDOUTQ) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Output Queue (DLTOUTQ) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with it. The Work
with Output Queue (WRKOUTQ) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Output Queue (RLSOUTQ) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Description
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to description it. The Work
with Output Queue Desc (WRKOUTQD) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Work with Writers
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to work with Writers it. The
Work with Writers (WRKWTR) command runs for the entry.
:PT.14=Clear
:PD.Type 14 next to an entry and press Enter to clear it. The Clear
Output Queue (CLROUTQ) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/FILEKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F11=View 2
:PD.View 2.
:PT.F11=View 1
:PD.View 1.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F20=Writers
:PD.Runs WRKWTR.
:PT.F22=Printers
:PD.Runs WRKWTR.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILES/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FILE'.File
:P.The file, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USRDTA'.User Data
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STS'.Sts
:P.The sts of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PAGES'.Pages
:P.The pages of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/COPIES'.Copies
:P.How many copies are printed.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FORMTYPE'.Form Type
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PTY'.Pty
:P.The pty of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOB'.Job
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NUMBER'.Number
:P.The number of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILES/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Send
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to send it. The Send Network
Spooled File (SNDNETSPLF) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Spooled File Attr (CHGSPLFA) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Spooled
File (HLDSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Spooled File (DLTSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Spooled File (DSPSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Spooled File (RLSSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Messages
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to messages it. The Display
Messages (DSPMSG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Attributes
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to attributes it. The Work
with Spooled File Attributes (WRKSPLFA) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Work with printing status
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to work with printing status
it. The Work with Writers (WRKWTR) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
